  "highlight": "Michael Renford crossed the English Channel from England to France in 12 hours 10 minutes on 1 August 2007.",
  "biography": [
    "Renford followed his father Des into long-distance swimming. In January 2025 Michael swam 34 kilometres down Tasmania’s Derwent River from New Norfolk to Hobart, fifty years after Des completed the route. His own Channel swim in 2007 was escorted by Dave Whyte on Ocean Breeze.",
    "The English Channel swim on 1 August 2007 took 12 hours 10 minutes. The Catalina federation records 9 hours 13 minutes 22 seconds on 5 September 2011. In New York the 6 June 2009 Manhattan circuit took 7 hours 29 minutes 4 seconds."
